  ok   the runtime and baked vertices correspond 1:1, and their normals differ only ON the cut — 11779 kept vertices, 0 unmatched; 127 on the cut diverge up to 16.365°, off the cut 0.0316° — which is why the corner key is position + UV and NOT normal

--- 9.2 RED: three mechanisms, one defect class ---
  ok   RED 1: hide masks absent (export_attributes off) is caught — 26756 triangles, the whole body, against the baked 21380
  ok   RED 2: the all-three-vertices keep rule is caught — 21626 triangles against the baked 21380, 246 too many
  ok   RED 3: the corrupted mask flags the same number of vertices AND yields the same count — hid vertex 550 instead of 1486, both move 1 triangles; count 21380 = baked 21380
  ok   RED 3: and the centroid clause catches it where the count clause cannot — 1 triangles in the rebuild that are not in the bake

--- 9.2 RED: winding and seam twins, both invisible to count and centroid ---
  ok   RED 4: reversed winding — the COUNT and CENTROID clauses both read GREEN on it — 21380 triangles, centroid multiset identical to the bake; this is why those two clauses alone were a decoration
  ok   RED 4: the ORIENTED CORNER clause catches it — every triangle, not a sample — 21380 of 21380 triangles differ from the bake
  ok   RED 4: and the intrinsic FACING clause catches it independently, with no bake to compare to — 21380/21380 triangles face inward, worst dot -1.000000 against +0.263262 when correct
  ok   RED 5: a UV-seam twin — COUNT, CENTROID and FACING all read GREEN on it — 21380 triangles, centroid multiset identical, facing worst dot 0.263262 byte-identical to the correct rebuild's
  ok   RED 5: only the ORIENTED CORNER clause catches it, because only its key carries UV — corner 524 -> its twin 525 (same position, same normal, UV 0.4468 away); 3 of 3 touched triangles differ from the bake

